HST Office: PPTX slide transitions round-trip like the reference presentation app writes them.

- Export: a transition duration is written only together with an effect. Slides without an effect no longer
  gain an empty <p:transition spd="slow" p14:dur="2000"/> carrying the 2 s default duration of SdPage. The
  transition element is still written for an advance timing or a transition sound alone.
- Import: an advance timing without an effect (<p:transition advTm="3000"/>) now makes the slide advance
  automatically; it was dropped unless a p14:dur happened to be present.
- A plain <p:cut/> (no thruBlk) is imported as an instant change (no effect) with a zero duration, and the
  export writes such a slide back as <p:cut/> instead of dropping the element. Cut through black is unchanged.
- sd/qa: export and round-trip tests for the three cases.

